Follow [Build AI agents with AI Gateway and AI SDK](https://vercel.com/kb/guide/ai-gateway-and-ai-sdk) to set up authentication, stream responses, and add tools and model fallbacks.

Vercel Connect supplies short-lived OAuth tokens to MCP clients built with AI SDK, so models can call tools from services such as Linear without storing provider credentials in your application. The `connectAuthProvider()` helper requests credentials and supports user consent flows.

Follow the [AI SDK and MCP tutorial](https://vercel.com/docs/connect/frameworks/ai-sdk-and-mcp) to configure Vercel Connect, make MCP tools available to an AI SDK application, and handle tool approval.

[Jev](https://vercel.com/kb/jev-from-typesafe-ai), a decision model from TypeSafe AI, returns typed choices, scores, and boolean probabilities that your application can use to classify requests, route work, and assess proposed actions. Call Jev through AI Gateway with the experimental `decide` API in `ai` 7.0.128 or later. The previous `experimental_evaluate` export still works as a deprecated alias.

Learn how to [classify, route, and score with Jev and AI SDK](https://vercel.com/kb/guide/typesafe-jev-and-ai-sdk), or follow [Route form submissions with Jev and AI SDK](https://vercel.com/kb/guide/jev-ai-sdk-form-router) to build a form router with configurable destinations and a fallback model for uncertain decisions.

